        ✔ Replace circle with animated energy orb @done(26-05-30 16:55)
            ✔ Option A — Particle system (pure OpenCV/numpy, no external assets needed) @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Emit "sparks" from the orb center each frame: each particle has (x, y, vx, vy, life, color) @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Update positions with velocity each frame, fade alpha by life remaining @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Use additive blending (cv.add or addWeighted with high src2 weight) so particles stack @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Spawn rate and velocity spread driven by time-in-charge for a build-up feel @done(26-05-30 16:55)
            ✔ Option B — Sprite sheet (easiest path to good-looking results) @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Find or render a looping orb animation as a PNG sequence (Blender, VFX assets) @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Store frames in assets/hollow_purple/ @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Each frame must have an alpha channel (BGRA) for transparent overlay @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Composite with: frame[mask] = sprite[mask], or cv.addWeighted on the ROI @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Advance frame index at a fixed rate (e.g. every 2 camera frames = ~15 fps animation) @done(26-05-30 16:55)
            ✔ Option C — OpenGL shader (best quality, most work) @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Use moderngl to render a glow/distortion shader to an offscreen texture @done(26-05-30 16:55)
                ✔ Convert texture to numpy array, alpha-blend onto the OpenCV frame @done(26-05-30 16:55)
