✔ Stage 4 (Sukuna's Cleave — second jutsu) @done(26-06-23)
✔ Stage 4.1 (Cleave refinements & bug fixes) @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Bug: service.py was passing ACTIVE_JUTSU list directly to jutsu_registry.load() — pipeline crashed immediately when Discord opened camera @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Bug: main.py never called init_audio() — cleave sound never initialized @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Bug: direction was distorted in normalized [0,1] coords due to aspect ratio (atan2 gave wrong angle) — reverted to pixel coords, normalize threshold by frame width instead @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Bug: rotation-and-crop approach clipped diagonal slashes — for 45° angle slash only reached middle of top/bottom edges, not corners — replaced with Python geometry (draw from frame boundary to frame boundary) @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ FlickDetector rewrite — palm centroid of 6 base joints instead of wrist alone; speed in px/s (time-based, fps-independent); separate speed window (80 ms) and direction window (40 ms) @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ EMA smoothing (α=0.40) on palm centroid — damps single-frame jitter spikes to 40% while real multi-frame flicks lose only ~20% of peak speed; allows threshold to be lowered safely @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Jump filter — single-frame centroid teleport > 18% of frame width discarded as tracking artifact; buffer preserved so next real sample continues cleanly @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Direction consistency gate — 80 ms speed vector and 40 ms direction vector must agree within 90°; wildly divergent vectors indicate mid-window jitter, suppresses false triggers @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Cleave audio — plays cleave.wav from assets/cleave/audio/ on every on_flick() call; scans directory for any audio file so filename doesn't matter @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ watcher.py — auto-reloads service.py 1 second after any .py file changes; setup_autostart.py now registers watcher.py instead of service.py @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Hollow Purple audio volume tuning (charge 0.025, release 0.0875, vmm release 0.79) @done(26-06-23)


    ✔ Multi-jutsu support — ACTIVE_JUTSU changed from str to list[str]; main loop iterates list and collects all detectors @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Camera fps — camera/feed.py now tries 60 fps before falling back to 30 fps @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Cleave gesture detection — pure velocity-based, no ML model @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ FlickDetector: time-based speed (px/s), fps-independent, 80 ms look-back window @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ Dual-mode: wrist-body flick (≥600 px/s) OR finger-only flick (≥450 px/s with wrist speed <180 px/s) @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ 60 ms minimum between triggers — rapid succession legal, same-motion echo blocked @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Chain slash — CleaveState holds a list of concurrent active slashes; on_flick() always appends, never blocks @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Effect duration is time-based (270 ms via time.monotonic), not frame-count-based — works at any fps @done(26-06-23)
    ✔ Cleave visual effect — manga-style B&W ink slash @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ 8-frame RGBA PNG sequence rendered in Blender 5.1 (1024×1024, horizontal, transparent background) @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ Shape: thin outer black blade (curved lens, ~22 px) + inner white core (linear wedge, ~7 px) @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ Blade extends well off-screen (half_w=2.5) — reads as consistent-width line across full frame @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ Animation: white core appears frame 1, black ink wraps in frame 2, both fade by frame 8 @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ Python renderer rotates 1024×1024 frame to match flick angle, center-crops to camera frame @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ Perpendicular shear displacement (±10 px, peak at t=0) gives "world sliced" feel @done(26-06-23)
        ✔ 40 spark particles scatter along cut line and fade over effect duration @done(26-06-23)

